    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "musig: allocate scratch space for multi-exponentiation in pubkey_agg",
    "user": {
      "login": "Yudis-bit",
      "id": 85178972,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTc4OTcy",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85178972?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Yudis-bit",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Yudis-bit/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "In `secp256k1_musig_pubkey_agg`, `secp256k1_ecmult_multi_var` is called with a NULL scratch space. Without a scratch space, `secp256k1_ecmult_multi_var` falls back to `secp256k1_ecmult_multi_simple_var`, which evaluates each public key scalar multiplication individually in a serial loop with up to 129 point doublings per signer.\n\nThis patch addresses the TODO in `secp256k1_musig_pubkey_agg` by allocating a temporary scratch space sized for Strauss (or Pippenger when n_pubkeys exceeds `ECMULT_PIPPENGER_THRESHOLD`). By providing the scratch buffer, `secp256k1_ecmult_multi_var` executes multi-scalar multiplication sharing the point doubling loop across the entire signer set.\n\nIn local benchmarks on x86_64, this cuts pubkey aggregation cycles by roughly 34% for 4 signers (274k vs 416k cycles), 57% for 16 signers (998k vs 2.37M cycles), and 58% for 128 signers (7.27M vs 17.39M cycles, saving over 10M cycles per call). All existing MuSig2 test vectors and module tests pass.\n",
